Now write the continuous expansion $\ket{\Psi}
=
\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}
\psi(x')\ket{x'}\,dx'.$ Acting with $\bra{x}$ gives $\begin{aligned}
\braket{x}{\Psi}
&=
\int dx'\,\psi(x')\braket{x}{x'} \notag\\
&=
\int dx'\,\psi(x')\delta(x-x') \notag\\
&=
\psi(x).
\end{aligned}$ Thus the coefficient in the expansion and the projection $\braket{x}{\Psi}$ are the same function, exactly as in a discrete basis.

